From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +000
Subject: [PATCH] Cast video memory pointers returned through libretro API

retro_get_memory_data returns byte-addressable memory as void *. PicoDrive's
VRAM and CRAM arrays are stored as 16-bit words, so GCC 15 rejects assigning
them directly to the local uint8_t pointer.

Cast these two memory regions explicitly before returning them.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
---
 platform/libretro/libretro.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/libretro/libretro.c b/platform/libretro/libretro.c
index 6d8e7ef..dc008b2 100644
--- a/platform/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/platform/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -1680,10 +1680,10 @@ void *retro_get_memory_data(unsigned type)
             data = PicoMem.ram;
          break;
       case RETRO_MEMORY_VIDEO_RAM:
-         data = PicoMem.vram;
+         data = (uint8_t *)PicoMem.vram;
          break;
       case 4:
-         data = PicoMem.cram;
+         data = (uint8_t *)PicoMem.cram;
          break;
       default:
          data = NULL;
-- 
